		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A `for` header's own declarator is a declarator: its `=` takes the same assignment",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 105
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " layout the statement-level one takes, so an over-width initializer breaks after the",
			"start": 107,
			"end": 193
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " `=` and its continuation is indented one level.",
			"start": 195,
			"end": 245
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " 100 - the declarator fits on the clause line",
			"start": 248,
			"end": 295
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " 101 - one char longer: the value drops below the `=`",
			"start": 435,
			"end": 490
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " the value's own operators break under that same indent when the continuation overflows",
			"start": 634,
			"end": 723
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " a call initializer expands its arguments rather than breaking after the `=`",
			"start": 882,
			"end": 960
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " the call-object clause holds here too: a lone `.prop` off a call WITH ARGUMENTS",
